# --- ODP recommendation use case ---------------------------------------------
# The generic `.cache` rule above would drop the shipped ontology-text cache.
# That file is a deliberate part of the release: it lets the stored
# recommendation results be reproduced without re-parsing every ontology.
!use-cases/odp-recommendation/recobench/.cache/
!use-cases/odp-recommendation/recobench/.cache/noOBO_text.json
# Fine-tuned encoder checkpoints are regenerable (Phase 5) and large (~88 MB).
use-cases/odp-recommendation/recobench/.cache/ft_*/

# --- release: data lives on Zenodo, not in git -------------------------------
# The corpus is ~2.7 GB and contains files above GitHub's 100 MB hard limit
# (cco.owl, go.owl, mondo-simple.owl, upheno.owl, zp.owl). Git is the wrong
# store for it: every version would be kept forever in history.
#
# Git tracks the SMALL, TEXTUAL, DIFFABLE part -- the views, the manifest, the
# audit -- so changes between versions are reviewable in a pull request.
# Zenodo holds the corpus, versioned under one concept DOI.
release-*/corpus/
release-*/*-hashed/
release-*/views/*-hashed/

# --- credentials: never commit -----------------------------------------------
cred.txt
**/cred.txt
.env
*.key

# --- SAGE LaTeX template ---------------------------------------------------
# sagej.cls and the SageV/SageH .bst files are redistributed by SAGE under an
# explicit restriction: "This software may only be used to prepare an article
# for publication in a SAGE Publications journal. Any other use constitutes an
# infringement of copyright."  This repository is public, so the class is kept
# locally for compiling but NOT committed.  Get it from:
#   https://uk.sagepub.com/sites/default/files/sage_latex_template_4.zip
paper-iri/sagej.cls
paper-iri/Sage*.bst
paper-iri-label/sagej.cls
paper-iri-label/Sage*.bst
docs/sage-template/

